+# AETHELIOS RESERVE — prefilm rehearsal
+
+This is a browser rehearsal of the actual Atelier application, not a film, deployed site, operating store, live provider run or production acceptance. Application source is recorded in results.json. The name is **AETHELIOS RESERVE** throughout Discovery and the saved business profile. No Legacy Reserve substitution was used.
+
+## Repeatable click path
+
+1. Open the public `/` homepage. Click its **Explore your direction** CTA, then Discovery's **Explore your direction**.
+2. Enter **AETHELIOS RESERVE**. Choose **Not sure yet** for business type, **Present the work more clearly**, and enter: “Full brand and existing-identity extension: supplier-backed catalogs, sourcing coordination, managed commerce. Planning only.” Choose Calm and a quality, then **Open the studio**.
+3. Click **Compare two**, refine the headline to **Considered sourcing** and the palette to Ivory Hall, then **Use Lumen**. Click **Continue in Studio**, follow the sign-in link and choose the clearly labeled local simulated owner.
+4. In Business, explicitly save the name **AETHELIOS RESERVE**, the planning-only services and the note that official logo originals are unavailable. Return to Studio. Choose **Direction → Continue existing identity → Lock and save direction**.
+5. In Refine/Text, use headline **Considered sourcing** and concise body **AETHELIOS RESERVE · Planning study**. In Image, retain the full planning intent as direction, with official-logo unavailability stated. Select Direction board, then **New draft**. Switch between Direction board, Square social and Website banner; use **Export** for each. Export saves the corresponding editable revision first.
+6. Click header **Simulated owner → Sign out**. Reopen the exact saved Studio URL including its query, click sign-in and choose the local owner. Confirm saved identity/copy, then **Image → Composition exports · download only → Download exported revision** for each file.
+
+The automated run also includes a separate negative/recovery exercise before step 5: the longer 87-character service body exceeds the direction-board text area. The interface reports overflow rather than silently clipping. The operator explicitly replaces it with the short body above, saves and reopens. This is an authoring constraint, not an unexplained smooth-path success. The full business intent remains in Discovery, Business and the saved image direction.
+
+## Evidence and visual limits
+
+All primary captures are normal viewport screenshots at 1440×900, 884×900 and 390×844. Supplemental homepage and Collection captures use 1920×1080. Three artifact PNGs use native dimensions. Results distinguish authenticated fetch/pixel checks from actual browser-download-button files retained under downloads/.
+
+The selected art uses Atelier's disclosed curated architecture studies. These are **not AETHELIOS RESERVE product/catalog assets**, supplier inventory or evidence of an operating commerce service. Exact lettering remains an editable text layer; no official Reserve logo was invented.
+
+The supplied originals remain blocked independently of browser success. Library prepared both originals, but the supported download GET returned HTTP403 from the environment proxy for each: `libfile_9a9a792423948191ab1e6d6755bca344` (3030.png) and `libfile_518437ba28c08191baf694d497144b21` (3029.png). No bytes were obtained and expected hashes could not be verified. No alternate ZIP retry or substitute logo was used. See asset-transfer-audit.json. The merged public Atelier logo is a separate asset and is not the Reserve identity.
+
+Font inspection confirms fallback rendering locally: homepage headline Liberation Serif and body/eyebrow Noto Sans; requested Cormorant/Figtree faces did not load. See font-audit.json. The compositor uses portable explicit canvas fonts. Production typography and the original Reserve-logo path are not accepted by this rehearsal.
+
+Local SQLite and explicitly simulated authentication only. No video, deployment, push, hosted database change, credential setup, paid operation or live AI call occurred. Hosted authentication/Postgres/provider behavior remains unverified.
+
+## Recorded outcome
+
+Application source: `99a7524d60b13f2c6a6579a5cea2913e08c71d27`. **56 main checks passed, 0 failed**; **2 cinematic viewport checks passed, 0 failed**. No browser console/hydration errors. Three decoded preview/export comparisons had maximum channel difference0. Three retained-file hashes matched before/after authentication, and all three actual UI download files matched their retained hashes. The saved BrandKit (including retained references) and palette were identical after signing back in; no logo layer or official identity asset was fabricated.
+
+The final9 format screenshots were recaptured after Export completed, using the same saved copy and identity, to exclude transient disabled/exporting controls. The supplementary script re-saved those formats, preserving previous exported revisions. Main results retain the original verified revision IDs and downloaded filenames.
+
+Manual review covered the real homepage, mobile Discovery controls, desktop board, phone announcement, fold banner and1920Collection. Captures show the exact Reserve name and readable short copy; cinematic Collection displays all three real compositions. Original-logo and production-font limitations above remain blockers for an original-identity/production-visual rehearsal.
+
+Package: 36 PNG files, including3native exports and3actual browser-downloaded copies, with SHA256/source manifest. Root's unit suite reports261passed/15skipped; typecheck passed. These local results do not confer launch acceptance.
